editorialMd:
The working idea

The input contains two rows: a sorted drawer and query values. For each query, produce the first index whose drawer value is at least that query; use the drawer's length if no such index exists.

Return the entire derived sequence, preserving its order.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(q log(n+1)); space O(n).

javascript
function insertionTabsProofStrip(drawers, k) {
  const a=drawers; let out=[];
  for(const x of a[1]){let l=0,r=a[0].length;while(l<r){const m=Math.floor((l+r)/2);if(a[0][m]<x)l=m+1;else r=m;}out.push(l);}
  return out;
}


